WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
1 million young Britons outside work or training lead the prime minister to call it catastrophe. This is Omni View, episode 210. Britain's prime minister tied the warning to people staying out of the labor market for the long term, and to how support for young people differs by region. BBC reporting presents the comments as a direct response to official figures on young people outside employment, education, or training. He also called the situation a moral failure. The Guardian places the statement alongside comments from

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.960
the Children's Commissioner on regional inequalities in support for young people.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:39.660
That coverage also includes opposition proposals for targeted energy bill cuts and hospitality

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.800
tax reductions.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.960
Comments from the Children's Commissioner set next to the statement in that coverage, stress

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.100
support systems that differ by region rather than a single uniform service.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.020
The Prime Minister linked wealth creation with social justice measures.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:58.860
In his account, creating wealth and repairing fairness are meant to be pursued together

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:04.200
through work and training, not treated as a trade-off. Opposition voices want more

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.880
far-reaching help for vulnerable households, caped in time, and they would fund it with

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.420
windfall taxes on banks and energy operators. Their cases that energy bills, hospitality

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:20.620
taxes, and fuel costs should be eased first and only for a defined stretch of time. One

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.360
measure is an essential energy guarantee that would take 100 pounds off average annual

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:33.220
electricity and gas bills. They would lower hospitality value-added tax or VAT from 20% to 15%.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:38.660
Fuel duty would fall by 10% for the first three months. The bill would be met by taking back

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:44.400
excess support from monopoly energy operators and buy a one-off windfall tax on bank profits

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:50.137
that were unexpected. Subsea cables around the Philippines need streamlined government approvals

00:01:50.137 --> 00:01:54.437
and better coordination among agencies, so they can be maintained and repaired.

00:01:54.897 --> 00:01:58.817
According to PLDT, the country's largest telecommunications company.

00:01:59.457 --> 00:02:03.757
South China Morning Post reporting highlights industry warnings that repaired delays and

00:02:03.757 --> 00:02:08.317
limited monitoring could deter investment in the archipelago's digital infrastructure.

00:02:09.357 --> 00:02:14.577
Executives and analysts said current slow processes and fragmented oversight risk undermining

00:02:14.577 --> 00:02:17.197
the country's goal of becoming a regional digital hub.

00:02:17.197 --> 00:02:21.897
The comments came at a forum on archipelagic governance for subsea cables.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:28.077
PLDT highlighted the need for greater cooperation among government agencies and further reforms

00:02:28.077 --> 00:02:30.397
to expand that vital digital infrastructure.

00:02:30.937 --> 00:02:36.157
The paper frames the issue as a gap between stated policy ambitions and administrative capacity.

00:02:36.857 --> 00:02:41.517
The telco industry wants the country to become a regional digital hub anchored by stable

00:02:41.517 --> 00:02:42.637
underwater cables.

00:02:42.637 --> 00:02:47.677
A leading executive and analyst warned that slow approvals for repairs could undermine

00:02:47.677 --> 00:02:48.417
that ambition.

00:02:49.211 --> 00:02:54.271
Human Rights Watch reported that Mollie's armed forces and allied Russia-linked paramilitaries

00:02:54.271 --> 00:02:56.891
killed and wounded civilians in attacks and detention.

00:02:57.731 --> 00:03:02.591
Al Jazeera's account presents the findings as evidence of violations of international humanitarian

00:03:02.591 --> 00:03:06.011
law by multiple parties in Mollie's long-running conflict.

00:03:06.691 --> 00:03:10.431
Opposition armed groups also carried out unlawful killings and torture.

00:03:10.431 --> 00:03:15.371
The report was based on interviews conducted between late July and mid-September.

00:03:15.911 --> 00:03:20.211
It documented two apparently indiscriminate drone attacks by the Mollion military.

00:03:20.931 --> 00:03:25.151
A July 29 attack in the Kedal region destroyed part of a health facility.

00:03:25.751 --> 00:03:30.971
An August 19 attack on a market in the central region of Bandeagara killed six civilians

00:03:30.971 --> 00:03:32.411
and wounded at least 20.

00:03:33.031 --> 00:03:37.831
The report also documented an operation in the Sego region where Mollion soldiers shot

00:03:37.831 --> 00:03:39.031
and killed five girls.

00:03:39.031 --> 00:03:44.611
goals. In the central region of Mopty, members of the military allied Dozo militia killed three

00:03:44.611 --> 00:03:50.690
civilians. The watchdog called for the African Union to intervene more actively. Palestinians

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:55.930
and Gaza faced an immediate cut in food assistance from the World Food Program because donor

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:01.070
contributions have not been sufficient. Reuters reporting states the cut follows documented

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:07.270
shortfalls in international funding pledges. The reduction covers 500,000 people. It takes

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.130
makes effect immediately amid ongoing needs in the territory.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:15.150
The agency's statement links the decision to the practical limits of its current resources.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.950
People already facing severe food insecurity in the territory are the ones affected.

00:04:20.997 --> 00:04:25.717
Export performance helped China grow faster than expected in the July to September period.

00:04:26.397 --> 00:04:32.917
Official data showed gross domestic product, or GDP, rose 4.5 percent above earlier forecasts

00:04:32.917 --> 00:04:35.137
in AP news and Al Jazeera accounts.

00:04:35.137 --> 00:04:40.637
months. The acceleration came amid an artificial intelligence or AI-driven boom in exports.

00:04:41.457 --> 00:04:46.157
Domestic consumer confidence and the property sector remained weak. Even as China makes

00:04:46.157 --> 00:04:51.777
strides in areas such as AI, much of its domestic economy is dragged down by gloomy consumer

00:04:51.777 --> 00:04:57.637
sentiment and a real estate slump. Analysts continue to watch whether external sales can offset

00:04:57.637 --> 00:05:03.177
slower household spending. Elon Musk said his companies would give away shares to the public.

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:11.817
BBC World News presents that pledge alongside Anthropics plan to create a public benefit fund ahead of a plan stock market listing.

00:05:12.477 --> 00:05:20.677
Musk's announcement comes after Anthropics pledge. Anthropics made that pledge ahead of what has been described as a blockbuster stock market listing.

00:05:21.357 --> 00:05:28.517
Both announcements are treated as moves by major AI firms to broaden ownership stakes before or alongside large-scale listings.

00:05:28.517 --> 00:05:32.017
The companies are preparing for significant market events.

00:05:32.967 --> 00:05:38.387
University administrators in Ghana ending their strike is progress worth knowing after direct

00:05:38.387 --> 00:05:39.587
talks with the government.

00:05:40.147 --> 00:05:44.467
Ghanaian Times reporting records the suspension as the outcome of those negotiations.

00:05:45.127 --> 00:05:50.387
The Ghana Association of University Administrators and the Technical University Senior Administrators

00:05:50.387 --> 00:05:53.287
Association had been on industrial action.

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:57.727
They suspended it once talks had addressed roughly 80% of their grievances.

00:05:57.727 --> 00:06:04.487
The two associations represent senior administrators at universities and technical universities across the country.

00:06:05.301 --> 00:06:09.881
To really understand how governments produce a count of young people outside work or study,

00:06:10.401 --> 00:06:13.581
you have to watch how two separate data streams are stitched together.

00:06:14.161 --> 00:06:17.001
A lot of coverage treats that share as a simple headcount.

00:06:17.681 --> 00:06:22.581
The figure is actually built by joining labor force surveys to enrollment records from schools.

00:06:23.201 --> 00:06:25.841
Those two sources are gathered on different calendars.

00:06:25.841 --> 00:06:29.161
They also use definitions of training that do not match.

00:06:29.661 --> 00:06:34.021
What you get is a snapshot, and a snapshot can move with the calendar of students leaving

00:06:34.021 --> 00:06:34.461
school.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:38.361
It can also move when the rules for recording an apprenticeship change.

00:06:38.961 --> 00:06:43.541
Statistical offices merge what people tell household surveyors about their current activity

00:06:43.541 --> 00:06:47.201
with administrative files on who is enrolled in school or college.

00:06:47.881 --> 00:06:50.441
Household surveys ask what a person is doing now.

00:06:51.101 --> 00:06:55.201
Enrollment files record whether that person is on the books at a school or college.

00:06:55.201 --> 00:06:59.421
Seasonal effects appear because many young people finish courses in the summer.

00:06:59.981 --> 00:07:03.321
They may then take several months to enter a job or further training.

00:07:03.841 --> 00:07:08.601
When a proposal is said to cut the total quickly, the test is whether it would change survey

00:07:08.601 --> 00:07:11.441
methods or change actual job creation incentives.

00:07:12.101 --> 00:07:14.101
Training itself is not a single thing.

00:07:14.661 --> 00:07:19.301
The label can cover formal apprenticeships, short courses, or unstructured learning on the

00:07:19.301 --> 00:07:19.561
job.

00:07:20.181 --> 00:07:22.801
Different countries set different thresholds for what counts.

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:28.971
cross-check labor market statistics against the original statistical agency release, rather

00:07:28.971 --> 00:07:33.851
than secondary summaries. Compare coverage that publishes the underlying survey questions

00:07:33.851 --> 00:07:39.507
with coverage that focuses on political reaction. When the next official youth employment release

00:07:39.507 --> 00:07:44.947
lands, read the footnotes on how training is defined, and line up the raw survey questions

00:07:44.947 --> 00:07:50.387
against the quarter before to see whether any drop is behavior or measurement. BBC coverage

00:07:50.387 --> 00:07:55.007
of the youth employment statement stays with the official figures the Prime Minister was answering,

00:07:55.447 --> 00:08:00.127
while the Guardian sets that statement beside the Children's Commissioner and the opposition's

00:08:00.127 --> 00:08:06.127
energy, VAT and fuel duty package. And Thropick's plan stock market listing is still the large

00:08:06.127 --> 00:08:11.827
market event these public benefit share pledges are built around. That wraps up today's omniview.

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:17.627
Remember, the best informed people read more than one perspective, and the calmest ones know that

00:08:17.627 --> 00:08:20.727
that most days, somewhere, something is quietly getting better.

